<title>POLAND: Polish yr/yr CPI 20.5 pct in August vs 20.4 July.</title>
<headline>Polish yr/yr CPI 20.5 pct in August vs 20.4 July.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish consumer prices rose 0.5 percent in August against a 0.1 percent fall in July, bringing year-on-year inflation up to 20.5 percent, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>CPI rose 11.9 percent in the January-August period, compared with a 12.9 percent rise in the same period last year.  </p>
<p> POLISH CONSUMER PRICES	AUGUST     JULY	AUGUST 1995</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	0.5	-0.1	    0.4</p>
<p> yr/yr change		     20.5	20.4	   25.4</p>
<p> services m/m change	     0.7	 1.5	    0.7</p>
<p> services yr/yr change	  19.2	19.2	   29.5</p>
<p> food prices m/m change	 -0.2	-1.9	   -1.4</p>
<p> food prices yr/yr change     21.0	19.6	   21.1</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
